# Network play by the host's address (docs/phase-network.md, stage N5), the host's side; net_join.kps is the other
# program's. tools/ci.sh runs both at once over the install, each the one host of its own map of 127.0.0.1's ports
# (this one --lan-map 42000:1:0, so its game list is UDP port 42000 and its game 42001), so no broadcast crosses and the
# joiner finds the game only by this host's address. The host creates the first map's melee game, waits in the chat
# room for the joiner and for the map to reach it (a joiner without the map downloads it: a phone, net_lan_join.kps),
# starts it and moves a worker; both programs log the shared hash at tick 400, which tools/ci.sh compares.
options originals
clock real
wait screen gluMain
click control gluMain.4
wait dialog gluGameMode and still
click control glugamemode.original
wait screen gluConn
click control gluConn.9
wait dialog gluPEdit and still
text "Host"
click control gluPEdit.1
wait screen gluLogin
click control glulogin.ok
wait screen gluJoin
click control gluJoin.15
wait screen gluCreat
wait seconds 1
click control gluCreat.12
wait screen gluChat
wait lobby.humans >= 2 within 120000
wait seconds 3
wait lobby.distributed == 1 within 300000
click control gluChat.7
wait game within 30000
log started tick units:0 units:1
wait tick >= 40
select worker 96
expect selected > 0
rclick center 160 96
wait tick >= 400 within 120000
log played tick sim.shared units:0 units:1
wait seconds 3
quit
